#basePath P3_CiscoTroutDecision_Docks
#include "Header.leaf"

:: Decide
@exposed
@trigger    OnLocationChanged
// "NONE" ensures no other threads are in-progress
// global:currentPhase == 3 ensures player is in phase 3
@when       global:currentThread == "NONE", global:currentPhase == 3, location == "FishingDocks"
@cutscene
// Lock all location on map
$call SetInThreadLocks()
$call DisableMapButton()
$call SetBackground("bg/fishing-docks-bg.png")


//checks to see if player has been to the decision point before 
$if global:ciscoFirst == false
       $if global:troutFirst == false
       {@}   
              You find your uncles hauling nets of fish from their boat onto the dock. 
              They seem exhausted, but that fades when they see you. 

       {@João}
              Querida, que bom te ver. <b>It's good to see you, darling.</b>
              What brings you back here?

       {@You} 
              I need some numbers, and I figure you'd be the best to ask. 
              Do you information on the populations of cisco and trout in the lake?

       {@João}
              I've been keeping track of the population for cisco. 
              Your uncle's been looking at trout. 
              Two heads are better than one, you know. 
              So ask whichever one of us you want to know about first.

       {@You}
              Hmm, let's see...

       $OnceChoice(P3_CiscoPop_Note.Start, Ask about cisco populations.)
       $OnceChoice(P3_TroutPop_Note.Start, Ask about trout populations.)
       $else
       {@}
              Your uncles are still hauling nets.
       {@João}
              Ready to talk to me?
       $OnceChoice(P3_CiscoPop_Note.Start, Ask about cisco populations.)
       $endif
$elseif global:troutFirst == false
       $if global:ciscoFirst == false
       {@}   
              You find your uncles hauling nets of fish from their boat onto the dock. 
              They seem exhausted, but that fades when they see you. 

       {@João}
              Querida, que bom te ver. 
              </b>It's good to see you, darling.</b>
              What brings you back here?

       {@You} 
              I need some numbers, and I figure you'd be the best to ask. 
              Do you information on the populations of cisco and trout in the lake?

       {@João}
              I've been keeping track of the population for cisco. 
              Your tio's been looking at trout. 
              Two heads are better than one, you know. 
              So ask whichever one of us you wanna know about first.

       {@You}
              Hmm, let's see...

       $OnceChoice(P3_CiscoPop_Note.Start, Ask about cisco populations.)
       $OnceChoice(P3_TroutPop_Note.Start, Ask about trout populations.)
       $else
       {@João}
              Your tio's waiting for you whenever you are.
       $OnceChoice(P3_TroutPop_Note.Start, Ask your uncle about trout populations.)
       $endif
$endif